{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מראה", :translit "mar'eh", :gloss "the vision"} {:he "גבריאל", :translit "gavri'el", :gloss "Gabriel"} {:he "חגור כמין פסיקיא של עור", :translit "chagur kemin pesikya shel or", :gloss "girded with a sort of leather apron"} {:he "מראה למשה תבנית המשכן ותבנית כל כליו", :translit "mareh lemoshe tavnit hamishkan vetavnit kol kelav", :gloss "showed Moses the pattern of the Tabernacle and the pattern of all its vessels"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מראה", :b "גבריאל"}], :frame {:text "Numbers Rabbah 12:10 records that Gabriel was girded in a garment like a craftsman's apron, made from the hide of a single animal, and in this attire he showed Moses the form of the Tabernacle and each of its vessels so that Moses could reproduce them. The Midrash derives this from Exodus 25:40 and Numbers 8:4, where Moses is told he was 'shown' (mar'eh) the pattern on the mountain.", :sources ["Numbers Rabbah 12:10" "Exodus 25:40" "Numbers 8:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וכן תעשו", :translit "vekhen ta'asu", :gloss "and so shall you make"} {:he "וכן תעשו דגדעון", :translit "vekhen ta'asu digid'on", :gloss "and so shall you make of Gideon"} {:he "נתן הלפידים בכדים", :translit "natan halapidim bakhadim", :gloss "he placed the torches in pitchers"} {:he "ובראש האשמורה התיכונה", :translit "uverosh ha'ashmoreh hatikhonah", :gloss "and at the beginning of the middle watch"} {:he "תורמין את המזבח", :translit "tormin et hamizbe'ach", :gloss "they would clear the ashes from the altar"} {:he "העבודה הראשונה", :translit "ha'avodah harishonah", :gloss "the first service"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וכן תעשו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gideon's battle parallels Tabernacle service: torches in pitchers recall the vessels; middle watch timing recalls the dawn altar service."}], :frame {:text "Judges 7:16–19 recounts that Gideon divided his three hundred men into three companies, gave each man torches inside pitchers, and attacked at the beginning of the middle watch. The Yoma 18a and Tamid 28b describe dawn procedures in the Temple, including the clearing of ashes from the altar (terumat hadeshen) as the first service of the day. The Ba'al HaTurim links the rare phrase 'and so shall you make' appearing in Exodus 25:9 with its only other occurrence in Judges 6:26 (Gideon's altar) to draw a structural parallel between Gideon's battle and the Tabernacle service.", :sources ["Judges 7:16-19" "Judges 6:26" "Yoma 18a" "Tamid 28b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "מראה", :a-value 246, :b "גבריאל", :b-value 246, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וכן תעשו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וכן תעשו", :refs ["Exodus 25:9" "Judges 7:17"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gideon's battle parallels Tabernacle service: torches in pitchers recall the vessels; middle watch timing recalls the dawn altar service.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:19:19.919762520Z", :model "glm-5.2"}